1
00:00:01,126 --> 00:00:03,294
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:11,219 --> 00:00:14,180
[Camia] <i>You're not Lily.</i>
<i>Lily's my daughter.</i>

3
00:00:14,264 --> 00:00:15,390
<i>I have to save her.</i>

4
00:00:15,473 --> 00:00:17,934
[Ivy] <i>If you want to see Lily again,</i>

5
00:00:18,018 --> 00:00:19,602
<i>we need to get out of here.</i>

6
00:00:19,686 --> 00:00:22,731
[Carlotta] <i>Diego found out</i>
<i>that Ivy is Lily.</i>

7
00:00:22,814 --> 00:00:24,774
-[Jepoy] <i>Nanny, Diego's here.</i>
-[Carlotta] <i>Stop him!</i>

8
00:00:24,858 --> 00:00:28,528
[Julio] <i>Where is Miss Aguas,</i>
<i>and what do you know about her?</i>

9
00:00:28,611 --> 00:00:29,571
<i>Answer me!</i>

10
00:00:29,654 --> 00:00:32,574
<i>Even if I knew where Ivy was,</i>
<i>I wouldn't tell you.</i>

11
00:00:32,657 --> 00:00:34,117
<i>You idiot!</i>

12
00:00:34,200 --> 00:00:36,786
<i>Try me. I'm not the same kid</i>
<i>you used to abuse.</i>

13
00:00:36,870 --> 00:00:39,789
[Ivy] <i>Mom, right now</i>
<i>we only have each other.</i>

14
00:00:39,873 --> 00:00:40,749
<i>Just you and me.</i>

15
00:00:40,832 --> 00:00:44,085
[Emilia] <i>Where are you going?</i>
<i>Are you leaving me? You bastard!</i>

16
00:00:44,169 --> 00:00:46,254
<i>When will you stop cheating on me?!</i>

17
00:00:46,337 --> 00:00:48,214
<i>Go on, do it. I'll burn her to ashes!</i>

18
00:00:48,298 --> 00:00:51,718
[Loring] <i>Fooling the Ardientes</i>
<i>like this is no joke.</i>

19
00:00:51,801 --> 00:00:53,970
<i>I'll sort all this out. I'll look for Ivy.</i>

20
00:00:54,054 --> 00:00:57,348
[Loring] <i>How will you find her?</i>
<i>Who knows where she is?</i>

21
00:00:57,432 --> 00:00:58,767
[Diego] <i>She's been missing</i>
<i>for a few days now,</i>

22
00:00:58,850 --> 00:01:00,435
<i>so please tell me where she is.</i>

23
00:01:00,518 --> 00:01:03,396
[man] <i>She went to the old Torillo house</i>
<i>here in San Ildefonso.</i>

24
00:01:03,480 --> 00:01:07,484
[Ivy] <i>Diego? Diego!</i>
<i>Diego, we're here! Diego!</i>

25
00:01:07,567 --> 00:01:10,153
[Emilia] <i>I'll find out</i>
<i>who your mistress is, Raul.</i>

26
00:01:10,236 --> 00:01:11,362
<i>Then you'll see.</i>

27
00:01:11,446 --> 00:01:13,573
[Ivy] <i>Raul's back again. Don't worry, Mom.</i>

28
00:01:13,656 --> 00:01:17,410
<i>I promise I'll find a way to get</i>
<i>out of here so we can find Lily.</i>

29
00:01:17,494 --> 00:01:20,580
[Raul] <i>But first, I'll sort our stuff out.</i>

30
00:01:20,663 --> 00:01:22,832
<i>-I'm hungry.</i>
<i>-You can talk now?</i>

31
00:01:22,916 --> 00:01:25,710
<i>You don't know how happy you've made me.</i>

32
00:01:25,794 --> 00:01:28,588
<i>I should buy us some food.</i>
<i>Then we'll celebrate, okay?</i>

33
00:01:28,671 --> 00:01:32,008
[Emilia] <i>One great move, Emilia. Good job.</i>

34
00:01:32,091 --> 00:01:33,802
[laughs]

35
00:01:33,885 --> 00:01:37,263
<i>Mom, wait! Mom!</i>

36
00:01:37,931 --> 00:01:40,683
-[Ivy] Mom! Mom!
-[Camia groaning]

37
00:01:42,977 --> 00:01:46,314
-Mom! Wait! Don't move!
-[fire whooshing]

38
00:01:46,397 --> 00:01:48,066
-Uh…
-[Camia coughing]

39
00:01:49,109 --> 00:01:50,360
[Ivy and Camia coughing]

40
00:01:50,443 --> 00:01:53,655
Come here. You can do it. Mom.

41
00:01:53,738 --> 00:01:55,281
[Camia coughing and panting]

42
00:01:55,365 --> 00:01:59,452
Come on, Mom. Don't be afraid. Come here.

43
00:01:59,536 --> 00:02:01,287
I'm right here, Mom. Don't be scared.

44
00:02:02,247 --> 00:02:03,581
[Ivy coughing]

45
00:02:03,665 --> 00:02:08,002
Mom. Hurry! We need to find Lily.

46
00:02:08,086 --> 00:02:10,588
Mom. [coughing]

47
00:02:12,048 --> 00:02:14,592
-Come here, Mom.
-[fire whooshes]

48
00:02:15,385 --> 00:02:18,263
-Mom.
-[Camia panting]

49
00:02:18,346 --> 00:02:19,681
This way, Mom.

50
00:02:20,390 --> 00:02:21,641
[Camia coughing]

51
00:02:23,685 --> 00:02:24,769
[Camia coughing]

52
00:02:25,603 --> 00:02:26,563
Hello, Raul?

53
00:02:27,355 --> 00:02:30,358
Come back here. I have a surprise for you.

54
00:02:30,441 --> 00:02:32,569
What are you talking about, Emilia?

55
00:02:32,652 --> 00:02:33,903
Where will I go back?

56
00:02:33,987 --> 00:02:36,698
Oh, come on, Raul! Where else?

57
00:02:36,781 --> 00:02:38,700
Your mistress' house, of course.

58
00:02:40,535 --> 00:02:41,619
[Camia coughs]

59
00:02:41,703 --> 00:02:43,163
[thumping]

60
00:02:43,955 --> 00:02:46,749
[Camia coughing]

61
00:02:46,833 --> 00:02:48,543
Aren't you going to see how she's doing?

62
00:02:49,335 --> 00:02:50,503
<i>Come on, Raul!</i>

63
00:02:50,587 --> 00:02:53,214
Do I have to spell it out for you?

64
00:02:53,673 --> 00:02:55,425
That would be so boring.

65
00:02:56,384 --> 00:03:00,054
<i>Just come back here</i>
<i>so you can see it for yourself.</i>

66
00:03:00,138 --> 00:03:06,019
It's only polite to say goodbye
before she burns in hell.

67
00:03:07,270 --> 00:03:09,022
[fire raging]

68
00:03:09,981 --> 00:03:14,152
You're a monster, Emilia!
Don't you dare do anything to her!

69
00:03:14,235 --> 00:03:15,862
Or else I will kill you!

70
00:03:15,945 --> 00:03:18,823
[laughs]

71
00:03:19,657 --> 00:03:21,451
[Ivy panting]

72
00:03:24,203 --> 00:03:26,789
[Raul] <i>When will you stop killing people?</i>

73
00:03:27,081 --> 00:03:28,917
When will you stop all this?

74
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:33,004
When will I stop? When will I stop?!

75
00:03:33,087 --> 00:03:35,632
Do you really want to know when, Raul?!

76
00:03:36,132 --> 00:03:39,636
When you finally stop cheating on me!

77
00:03:39,719 --> 00:03:43,097
[suspenseful music playing]

78
00:03:48,478 --> 00:03:49,520
[Camia coughs]

79
00:03:50,688 --> 00:03:51,731
Mom.

80
00:03:58,613 --> 00:04:00,490
-[Camia coughing]
-I'll go first, Mom. [grunts]

81
00:04:05,662 --> 00:04:06,788
-[Camia coughing]
-Mom.

82
00:04:10,083 --> 00:04:13,086
[suspenseful music continues playing]

83
00:04:16,130 --> 00:04:17,715
-[Camia coughing]
-Mom.

84
00:04:27,016 --> 00:04:28,518
[phone ringing]

85
00:04:30,395 --> 00:04:32,730
-Nanny Carlotta?
-[Carlotta] <i>Jepoy.</i>

86
00:04:32,855 --> 00:04:34,899
Do you have any news on Ivy?

87
00:04:35,149 --> 00:04:36,776
My gut's telling me that,

88
00:04:36,859 --> 00:04:38,569
if I find Raul, I'll find Ivy too.

89
00:04:38,653 --> 00:04:41,239
-Yeah.
-Emilia went to go look for him.

90
00:04:41,322 --> 00:04:43,324
So I'm going to follow her.

91
00:04:43,408 --> 00:04:45,410
But, Jepoy, a lot of people

92
00:04:45,493 --> 00:04:47,078
are watching your every move right now.

93
00:04:47,161 --> 00:04:48,997
<i>Especially Emilia.</i>

94
00:04:49,163 --> 00:04:52,417
Didn't you say that
you're her bodyguard now?

95
00:04:52,750 --> 00:04:57,547
<i>-Just be careful, Jepoy.</i>
-Yes, Nanny. I will. Bye.

96
00:05:01,676 --> 00:05:02,719
Madrigal.

97
00:05:04,804 --> 00:05:07,181
Where are you going? Didn't I
tell you to keep an eye on Mom?

98
00:05:08,433 --> 00:05:10,059
She's already sleeping, Mayor.

99
00:05:10,268 --> 00:05:13,521
So, I figured maybe I can spend
some time in town for a while.

100
00:05:15,064 --> 00:05:17,692
[tense music playing]

101
00:05:22,071 --> 00:05:23,823
-[Camia coughs]
-Just a little longer, Mom.

102
00:05:23,906 --> 00:05:25,074
We're almost there.

103
00:05:25,241 --> 00:05:26,784
[Camia coughing]

104
00:05:26,868 --> 00:05:29,162
We're safe now, Mom. Mom…

105
00:05:29,370 --> 00:05:31,914
-[Camia coughing]
-Mom…

106
00:05:31,998 --> 00:05:35,293
-Mom?
-[coughing]

107
00:05:35,376 --> 00:05:37,420
We've escaped the fire, Mom.

108
00:05:37,503 --> 00:05:38,880
Let's stay here, Mom.

109
00:05:39,589 --> 00:05:40,923
Mom? Mom!

110
00:05:44,802 --> 00:05:51,142
Mom! Mom! Mom? Mom?! Mom?

111
00:05:54,979 --> 00:05:55,980
Mom?

112
00:05:58,066 --> 00:06:00,359
[Ivy panting]

113
00:06:10,828 --> 00:06:12,663
[panting]

114
00:06:19,837 --> 00:06:24,175
Jasmin! Jasmin! Jasmin!

115
00:06:24,425 --> 00:06:27,095
[sobbing] Jasmin!

116
00:06:29,055 --> 00:06:30,348
Jasmin!

117
00:06:32,100 --> 00:06:37,355
Jasmin! Where are you, Jasmin?! Jasmin!

118
00:06:38,606 --> 00:06:42,235
[wailing] Jasmin!

119
00:06:43,319 --> 00:06:48,241
[wailing]

120
00:06:49,242 --> 00:06:52,870
Jasmin! I'm here, Jasmin!

121
00:07:01,170 --> 00:07:02,338
[grunting]

122
00:07:02,880 --> 00:07:05,466
[clapping and laughing]

123
00:07:06,467 --> 00:07:11,013
Poor thing. How long
have you been seeing each other?

124
00:07:11,681 --> 00:07:16,102
Two years? Five years? Or more?

125
00:07:16,894 --> 00:07:19,772
I bet it's more because
she must've meant a lot

126
00:07:19,856 --> 00:07:21,691
to you to act like that.

127
00:07:26,737 --> 00:07:31,993
So, Raul, do you love her more
than your first mistress?

128
00:07:32,285 --> 00:07:35,204
Does she make your insides quiver?

129
00:07:35,788 --> 00:07:38,583
Like, hmm… Camia?

130
00:07:41,252 --> 00:07:43,087
You remember her?

131
00:07:43,463 --> 00:07:45,798
The woman you used to lust after?

132
00:07:46,799 --> 00:07:51,888
From that family that just
disappeared back in Ardiente?

133
00:07:56,767 --> 00:07:57,852
Mom!

134
00:08:01,314 --> 00:08:06,652
[somber instrumental playing]

135
00:08:14,076 --> 00:08:17,079
Mom? Come on, Mom.

136
00:08:23,252 --> 00:08:26,964
Mom! Mom! Mom!

137
00:08:29,884 --> 00:08:30,885
Mom!

138
00:08:33,304 --> 00:08:34,305
Mom!

139
00:08:36,682 --> 00:08:39,810
[panics] Mom! Mom! No!

140
00:08:41,687 --> 00:08:43,564
Mom! Mom!

141
00:08:45,316 --> 00:08:46,359
Mom!

142
00:08:46,442 --> 00:08:48,361
-[Ivy sobbing]
-[Camia coughs]

143
00:08:48,444 --> 00:08:49,570
Mom!

144
00:08:50,279 --> 00:08:52,156
[crying] Mom… Mom.

145
00:08:55,243 --> 00:08:56,702
[screams]

146
00:08:58,454 --> 00:09:00,998
I thought you were
going to leave me again.

147
00:09:03,501 --> 00:09:06,337
[Ivy sobbing uncontrollably]

148
00:09:15,888 --> 00:09:20,518
[dramatic music playing]

149
00:09:26,399 --> 00:09:27,275
Diego?!

150
00:09:28,943 --> 00:09:31,529
Diego! Diego! Diego!

151
00:09:34,740 --> 00:09:36,367
-Diego!
-Ivy?

152
00:09:36,742 --> 00:09:38,869
Diego! Diego, help us, please!

153
00:09:39,996 --> 00:09:43,082
Diego, please!
My mother needs help, please!

154
00:09:43,541 --> 00:09:46,085
Diego, please! Diego!

155
00:09:47,878 --> 00:09:49,630
-Mom!
-Ivy, open the door!

156
00:09:50,256 --> 00:09:51,465
Hang on to me.

157
00:09:57,471 --> 00:09:58,681
Ivy, get in!

158
00:10:09,191 --> 00:10:10,901
You're a monster, Emilia!

159
00:10:11,444 --> 00:10:14,614
You're heartless! She was innocent!

160
00:10:15,865 --> 00:10:17,283
Why don't you just leave me alone?

161
00:10:17,617 --> 00:10:20,077
[giggles]

162
00:10:20,161 --> 00:10:21,662
Is your conscience bothering you?

163
00:10:21,746 --> 00:10:24,415
[Emilia laughing]

164
00:10:24,957 --> 00:10:26,584
It doesn't suit you, Raul.

165
00:10:27,251 --> 00:10:32,506
What you need to do is
stop lying and cheating on me.

166
00:10:32,590 --> 00:10:34,592
So we can spare other women from making

167
00:10:34,675 --> 00:10:37,011
an appointment with death!

168
00:10:37,094 --> 00:10:40,222
[laughs]

169
00:10:40,348 --> 00:10:41,515
Goodbye, Raul.

170
00:10:45,269 --> 00:10:46,896
You're a monster, Emilia!

171
00:10:46,979 --> 00:10:48,439
-[Emilia yelps]
-[Raul grunts]

172
00:10:48,522 --> 00:10:49,940
You're a heartless monster!

173
00:10:50,024 --> 00:10:53,527
-[Emilia yelps]
-I'll kill you, you animal!

174
00:10:53,736 --> 00:10:57,990
[Emilia yelping]

175
00:11:02,828 --> 00:11:04,622
-[Emilia grunting]
-[Raul] What?

176
00:11:05,414 --> 00:11:06,415
[coughs]

177
00:11:07,917 --> 00:11:09,001
You bitch!

178
00:11:09,085 --> 00:11:10,169
[Raul grunting]

179
00:11:10,753 --> 00:11:12,129
Ma'am, are you okay?

180
00:11:16,175 --> 00:11:17,760
Stay out of this, you little brat.

181
00:11:19,595 --> 00:11:22,098
I'm her bodyguard.
I won't let you hurt her.

182
00:11:22,723 --> 00:11:26,519
[suspenseful music playing]

183
00:11:26,894 --> 00:11:27,770
Step back.

184
00:11:28,646 --> 00:11:31,232
This isn't over. Keep that in mind.

185
00:11:33,109 --> 00:11:34,110
[exhales sharply]

186
00:11:34,652 --> 00:11:36,445
This isn't over, Emilia!

187
00:11:36,695 --> 00:11:39,573
[suspenseful music playing]

188
00:11:41,450 --> 00:11:42,451
[exhales]

189
00:11:45,663 --> 00:11:47,081
[car engine roars]

190
00:11:54,171 --> 00:11:55,214
Are you okay, Governor?

191
00:11:57,049 --> 00:12:01,470
-[fire crackling]
-[suspenseful music playing]

192
00:12:07,184 --> 00:12:09,645
Ivy, we're in San Ildefonso proper.

193
00:12:10,229 --> 00:12:13,607
But I can't see a hospital anywhere.

194
00:12:14,358 --> 00:12:16,527
Let's just bring her to your place.

195
00:12:17,111 --> 00:12:20,739
-No. Mom won't be safe there.
-What?

196
00:12:21,490 --> 00:12:25,786
Let's go to San Joaquin. Take us there.

197
00:12:25,870 --> 00:12:27,079
My mom will be safe there.

198
00:12:27,163 --> 00:12:28,873
-San Joaquin?
-Yes.

199
00:12:28,956 --> 00:12:31,333
In Bataan? Ivy,
that's an hour away from here.

200
00:12:31,417 --> 00:12:33,627
I don't care. Bring us to San Joaquin.

201
00:12:33,711 --> 00:12:36,922
I have property there.
Mom will be safe there. Please.

202
00:12:38,382 --> 00:12:39,592
Please.

203
00:13:00,279 --> 00:13:04,325
[Julio] Didn't I tell you not to go out?

204
00:13:05,159 --> 00:13:10,915
I said you couldn't leave this house
without my permission.

205
00:13:12,082 --> 00:13:14,752
But, Papa, Raul has a mistress.

206
00:13:14,835 --> 00:13:18,297
Your marital problems bore
the hell out of me, Emilia.

207
00:13:19,381 --> 00:13:22,259
If you find it boring, Papa,
well, for me, it's not.

208
00:13:22,343 --> 00:13:25,095
This is my family. I have to
do everything to save this.

209
00:13:25,679 --> 00:13:27,556
[Julio] Too late.

210
00:13:27,640 --> 00:13:30,768
There's nothing to save
as far as your marriage is concerned.

211
00:13:31,352 --> 00:13:35,022
Because your marriage
is as rotten as trash.

212
00:13:35,105 --> 00:13:38,234
But you're the one who said
I should solve all my problems.

213
00:13:38,317 --> 00:13:39,818
That's why I'm trying to fix this.

214
00:13:40,778 --> 00:13:41,904
In my world,

215
00:13:42,863 --> 00:13:47,576
I have lots of solutions
and answers to problems.

216
00:13:48,160 --> 00:13:52,957
But as for you, you only know
how to do one thing.

217
00:13:53,040 --> 00:13:55,501
Your only solution is to kill.

218
00:13:56,252 --> 00:14:01,507
But then again, what should
I expect from someone like you?

219
00:14:05,219 --> 00:14:06,595
I have no time for your worthless sermons.

220
00:14:06,679 --> 00:14:07,680
Raul!

221
00:14:08,097 --> 00:14:09,974
Ow! Papa.

222
00:14:10,975 --> 00:14:12,142
Remember this.

223
00:14:13,769 --> 00:14:17,439
If you allow that bastard
to keep treating you that way…

224
00:14:18,732 --> 00:14:22,236
I will make your life a living hell.

225
00:14:25,573 --> 00:14:28,742
You're just like your mother.
A willing victim.

226
00:14:29,159 --> 00:14:33,831
The emotional punching bag
of a useless man.

227
00:14:34,081 --> 00:14:37,585
-But I love Raul, Papa!
-Well, I have news for you!

228
00:14:39,086 --> 00:14:42,381
Love is only for those who deserve it.

229
00:14:53,100 --> 00:14:54,226
Let's go, Mom.

230
00:14:58,188 --> 00:14:59,148
Excuse me, Grandpa.

231
00:15:04,236 --> 00:15:05,404
[exhales]

232
00:15:20,085 --> 00:15:21,128
Good morning, ma'am.

233
00:15:21,545 --> 00:15:23,756
-Mom.
-Go on. Help her. Help her.

234
00:15:23,839 --> 00:15:26,091
-[Ivy] Where are the nurses?
-Nurse! Hurry up!

235
00:15:26,175 --> 00:15:27,176
-Come on.
-[Diego] I'll carry her.

236
00:15:30,137 --> 00:15:31,263
[Ivy] Diego, be careful.

237
00:15:38,354 --> 00:15:40,230
-Where should I lay her?
-Over there, sir.

238
00:15:40,856 --> 00:15:42,566
-Miss Aguas, I'm Dr. Faustino.
-Hello, Doc.

239
00:15:42,650 --> 00:15:44,151
I'm the colleague of Dr. Martinez,

240
00:15:44,234 --> 00:15:46,320
Miss Prianka Aguas' doctor.

241
00:15:51,283 --> 00:15:53,786
Doctor, thank you for coming
on such short notice.

242
00:15:53,869 --> 00:15:57,081
Um, you said you and the patient
were trapped in a fire?

243
00:15:57,164 --> 00:15:59,541
Yes. Because of that, she lost
consciousness and collapsed.

244
00:15:59,625 --> 00:16:01,335
So, I had to revive her.

245
00:16:01,835 --> 00:16:03,587
It's definitely smoke inhalation

246
00:16:03,671 --> 00:16:05,172
that affected her lungs,

247
00:16:05,255 --> 00:16:06,882
that's why she's having trouble breathing.

248
00:16:06,966 --> 00:16:09,885
But, with some rest,
she'll be able to recover soon.

249
00:16:13,180 --> 00:16:16,392
[panting]

250
00:16:18,852 --> 00:16:20,354
[Dr. Faustino] So, when she's much better,

251
00:16:20,437 --> 00:16:23,524
we will treat her catatonic depression.

252
00:16:25,067 --> 00:16:25,901
Please, doctor.

253
00:16:26,944 --> 00:16:28,904
Do everything you can to treat my mother.

254
00:16:28,988 --> 00:16:30,447
Yes. We will do that.

255
00:16:30,864 --> 00:16:35,411
[tense music playing]

256
00:16:36,662 --> 00:16:37,788
Excuse me.

257
00:16:49,591 --> 00:16:50,759
Ivy, are you all right?

258
00:16:53,137 --> 00:16:54,847
Yes. I'm fine.

259
00:16:57,099 --> 00:16:59,643
-Ivy, you're hurt.
-It's just a small wound.

260
00:16:59,727 --> 00:17:01,687
It's fine. Thank you.

261
00:17:05,566 --> 00:17:07,026
Ivy, can we talk?

262
00:17:08,902 --> 00:17:13,907
About you, about Miss Camia,
and about Lily.

263
00:17:13,991 --> 00:17:18,287
[tender music playing]

264
00:17:27,004 --> 00:17:29,798
[nurse] Excuse me, Miss Ivy.
The doctor wants to talk to you.

265
00:17:32,885 --> 00:17:33,927
Excuse me.

266
00:17:56,867 --> 00:18:00,329
What if Ivy was inside that house?

267
00:18:00,662 --> 00:18:03,290
Don't say that. Let's not think that way.

268
00:18:03,373 --> 00:18:07,002
But you just said Raul often
went there, so maybe

269
00:18:07,086 --> 00:18:11,215
that's where Camia was! Both her and Ivy!

270
00:18:14,343 --> 00:18:15,803
[phone ringing]

271
00:18:17,471 --> 00:18:18,430
It's Ivy!

272
00:18:19,765 --> 00:18:20,849
-Hello, dear?
-Ivy?

273
00:18:20,933 --> 00:18:23,644
-Dear?
-Nanny Carlotta.

274
00:18:23,727 --> 00:18:25,229
Oh, Ivy!

275
00:18:25,854 --> 00:18:28,482
We were so worried about you.
Where are you?

276
00:18:28,565 --> 00:18:30,734
I'm here at Puerto Del Sol.

277
00:18:31,777 --> 00:18:33,195
[Carlotta] <i>What are you doing there?</i>

278
00:18:34,571 --> 00:18:37,241
Nanny Carlotta, I found my mom.

279
00:18:38,158 --> 00:18:43,122
Raul locked her up in a house.
We were trapped there…

280
00:18:43,789 --> 00:18:46,834
<i>and I couldn't call you</i>
<i>because my phone died.</i>

281
00:18:46,917 --> 00:18:48,585
There was no power supply there.

282
00:18:49,086 --> 00:18:52,548
When we were about to escape,
the house suddenly caught fire.

283
00:18:52,631 --> 00:18:55,843
But don't worry. We're both safe now.

284
00:18:55,926 --> 00:18:58,470
Mom just needs to recover here
in Puerto Del Sol.

285
00:18:59,263 --> 00:19:01,140
Ivy. Do you need any help there?

286
00:19:01,223 --> 00:19:04,226
I'm okay. My staff can take care of us.

287
00:19:05,853 --> 00:19:08,647
Besides, Diego's here too.

288
00:19:10,274 --> 00:19:11,984
He's the one who helped us.

289
00:19:12,943 --> 00:19:15,112
[Jepoy] <i>Diego? Ivy…</i>

290
00:19:15,529 --> 00:19:17,281
Does Diego know the truth about you?

291
00:19:18,448 --> 00:19:19,241
<i>Ivy?</i>

292
00:19:19,324 --> 00:19:21,243
-Ivy.
-All right.

293
00:19:21,326 --> 00:19:24,037
Dear. Just take care, okay?

294
00:19:24,121 --> 00:19:27,583
You know how much
we care about your safety.

295
00:19:28,750 --> 00:19:29,793
Thank you.

296
00:19:30,377 --> 00:19:35,340
[somber music playing]

297
00:19:43,348 --> 00:19:47,269
Ivy, please. I need to know the truth.

298
00:19:56,653 --> 00:19:59,156
I'm sorry. I'm sorry, Diego.

299
00:20:24,139 --> 00:20:28,810
I know I've been craving power,
Aunt Claire, because all my life,

300
00:20:28,894 --> 00:20:30,646
Papa deprived me of that.

301
00:20:31,563 --> 00:20:35,025
But I don't deserve
to be treated like this.

302
00:20:35,776 --> 00:20:39,321
Aren't you used to him yet?
You should know by now

303
00:20:39,404 --> 00:20:42,699
how to bounce back every time
you're treated that way.

304
00:20:42,783 --> 00:20:45,410
If I could kill Raul's mistresses,

305
00:20:45,494 --> 00:20:47,746
it means I can do anything, Aunt Claire.

306
00:20:48,163 --> 00:20:50,207
Even if it means killing my own father.

307
00:20:51,166 --> 00:20:53,585
You've tried that before,
and it didn't work.

308
00:20:53,669 --> 00:20:55,671
I can do it again, Auntie.

309
00:20:56,797 --> 00:21:00,592
Emilia. Emilia.

310
00:21:03,679 --> 00:21:06,473
The reason you can't outwit
your father is because

311
00:21:06,556 --> 00:21:07,891
you're too predictable.

312
00:21:09,101 --> 00:21:10,269
Why don't you agree

313
00:21:10,352 --> 00:21:13,105
with what he wants
instead of going against him?

314
00:21:13,855 --> 00:21:17,317
In order for you to get what you want…

315
00:21:17,818 --> 00:21:20,112
you need to play along
with Julio Ardiente.

316
00:21:24,825 --> 00:21:26,159
[unsettling music playing]

317
00:21:26,243 --> 00:21:27,327
[cries]

318
00:21:42,009 --> 00:21:44,219
[breathes deeply]

319
00:21:50,267 --> 00:21:54,938
[unsettling music playing]

320
00:21:57,566 --> 00:21:59,026
<i>I won't be long.</i>

321
00:21:59,609 --> 00:22:02,779
<i>Raul. Please come back.</i>

322
00:22:03,363 --> 00:22:07,117
[crying] <i>Jasmin! Jasmin!</i>

323
00:22:07,659 --> 00:22:12,497
<i>I'm here! Jasmin!</i>

324
00:22:28,263 --> 00:22:30,015
<i>Forgive me, Camia.</i>

325
00:22:32,267 --> 00:22:35,437
<i>Because of me,</i>
<i>Emilia had you killed twice.</i>

326
00:22:36,480 --> 00:22:39,274
<i>But unlike before,</i>
<i>I couldn't save you this time.</i>

327
00:22:42,152 --> 00:22:43,278
<i>Forgive me.</i>

328
00:22:49,576 --> 00:22:52,079
[tender music playing]

329
00:22:56,374 --> 00:22:59,836
-[Diego] <i>Is this Ivy?</i>
-[teacher] <i>Yes, that's her.</i>

330
00:23:10,680 --> 00:23:12,682
-[Ivy] <i>Diego!</i>
-[Diego] <i>Ivy?</i>

331
00:23:12,766 --> 00:23:17,104
<i>Diego! Help us, please!</i>
<i>My mother needs help, please!</i>

332
00:23:18,438 --> 00:23:23,360
<i>I have so much to ask you.</i>
<i>I need answers to my questions.</i>

333
00:23:25,028 --> 00:23:29,074
Please tell me everything.
I'll understand.

334
00:23:46,967 --> 00:23:48,468
[phone ringing]

335
00:23:50,428 --> 00:23:51,888
[phone ringing]

336
00:23:54,683 --> 00:23:56,101
Hello, Mr. Mayor?

337
00:23:57,144 --> 00:23:58,270
Grandpa, excuse me.

338
00:23:58,353 --> 00:24:01,064
Ivy, I'm so glad to hear from you.

339
00:24:01,148 --> 00:24:05,360
Don't make it too obvious
you missed me, Mr. Mayor.

340
00:24:05,443 --> 00:24:06,736
[Arnaldo] <i>Well, I won't deny that.</i>

341
00:24:06,820 --> 00:24:09,030
Besides, I was worried about you.

342
00:24:09,114 --> 00:24:11,074
I've been trying to reach you
for the past couple of days,

343
00:24:11,158 --> 00:24:12,325
but you won't pick up.

344
00:24:12,409 --> 00:24:15,579
Oh, thank you, Mr. Mayor.

345
00:24:15,662 --> 00:24:20,458
I appreciate your concern for me,
but now, you don't need

346
00:24:20,542 --> 00:24:24,129
to worry about me because I'm fine,
and we're talking.

347
00:24:24,212 --> 00:24:26,173
I think I would be more at ease
if I saw you.

348
00:24:27,465 --> 00:24:32,429
Mr. Mayor, I decided to leave
because I need some alone time.

349
00:24:32,512 --> 00:24:36,766
But you'd defeat its purpose
if you come to me, right?

350
00:24:37,475 --> 00:24:40,979
Okay, fine. I'll see you soon. Okay?

351
00:24:41,062 --> 00:24:41,897
[Ivy] <i>Of course.</i>

352
00:24:42,480 --> 00:24:45,108
I will see you soon, Mr. Mayor.

353
00:24:52,574 --> 00:24:57,621
-Well, where's Miss Aguas?
-She's soul-searching, Grandpa.

354
00:24:57,704 --> 00:25:00,123
Uh… But she said she'll come back soon.

355
00:25:00,207 --> 00:25:02,918
[scoffs] And you believed her?

356
00:25:05,670 --> 00:25:10,050
Arnaldo. You are the predator.

357
00:25:10,133 --> 00:25:13,762
And Miss Aguas is the prey.

358
00:25:15,096 --> 00:25:18,141
And predators are never soft.

359
00:25:19,601 --> 00:25:24,522
You need Miss Aguas for your candidacy.

360
00:25:28,151 --> 00:25:29,611
You heard me right.

361
00:25:30,987 --> 00:25:36,117
You'll be running for senator in my place.

362
00:25:38,703 --> 00:25:40,956
And you need Ivy.

363
00:25:41,539 --> 00:25:47,629
You need Ivy's money
for our plans to push through.

364
00:25:48,713 --> 00:25:54,552
So, sharpen your fangs, and
go and take down your prey.

365
00:26:04,062 --> 00:26:06,856
Ivy. Answer me right now.

366
00:26:08,775 --> 00:26:09,859
Are you Lily?

367
00:26:12,445 --> 00:26:14,281
Please answer me, Ivy.

368
00:26:14,364 --> 00:26:16,825
Are Ivy Aguas and Lily Cruz
the same person?

369
00:26:17,951 --> 00:26:20,245
[tender music playing]

370
00:26:27,919 --> 00:26:29,379
I believe you already know.

371
00:26:33,967 --> 00:26:38,888
Yes, Diego. I'm your old friend, I'm Lily.

372
00:26:38,972 --> 00:26:41,516
[tender music continues playing]

373
00:26:49,065 --> 00:26:54,279
[soft piano music playing]

374
00:26:55,739 --> 00:26:58,325
[breathes heavily]

375
00:26:59,326 --> 00:27:00,910
Why did you lie to me?

376
00:27:03,413 --> 00:27:04,873
I have my reasons.

377
00:27:05,373 --> 00:27:06,750
A lot of reasons.

378
00:27:08,835 --> 00:27:12,589
And even if I told you,
you wouldn't understand?

379
00:27:12,672 --> 00:27:17,719
Ivy! We're not kids anymore.
I'm not a kid.

380
00:27:17,802 --> 00:27:19,888
I can understand
whatever those reasons are!

381
00:27:19,971 --> 00:27:23,099
-I need an answer!
-And I can't give you one.

382
00:27:24,684 --> 00:27:25,727
No, Diego.

383
00:27:26,478 --> 00:27:29,522
Whatever your questions are,
I can't give you any answers.

384
00:27:31,358 --> 00:27:34,861
I'm thankful for the friendship we had.

385
00:27:34,944 --> 00:27:37,906
And I thank you for accepting Ivy.

386
00:27:38,073 --> 00:27:42,786
But now, we should just be happy
to see each other.

387
00:27:42,869 --> 00:27:44,120
That's that, Diego.

388
00:27:44,996 --> 00:27:47,999
I want to know why my friend lied to me.

389
00:27:49,667 --> 00:27:51,419
Why did you pretend to be someone else?

390
00:27:52,128 --> 00:27:53,922
I need to understand Lily.

391
00:28:08,645 --> 00:28:11,356
[nurse] Miss Aguas. It's Miss Camia.

392
00:28:11,940 --> 00:28:13,691
Why? What happened to her?

393
00:28:19,948 --> 00:28:23,368
[Ivy] Doctor. What happened to my mother?

394
00:28:23,451 --> 00:28:25,787
She had an acute urinary tract infection,

395
00:28:25,870 --> 00:28:27,497
which explains the stomach ache.

396
00:28:27,705 --> 00:28:30,959
But she's also showing signs of
malnutrition and renal failure.

397
00:28:31,042 --> 00:28:33,628
These are all complications
brought about by her condition,

398
00:28:33,711 --> 00:28:35,213
catatonic depression.

399
00:28:40,593 --> 00:28:43,513
Doctor, how bad is it?

400
00:28:44,347 --> 00:28:47,016
If her condition doesn't improve,

401
00:28:47,100 --> 00:28:49,102
there's a possibility of kidney failure.

402
00:29:03,366 --> 00:29:07,495
[somber music playing]

403
00:29:24,596 --> 00:29:25,597
Excuse me.

404
00:29:34,189 --> 00:29:35,023
Governor.

405
00:29:35,106 --> 00:29:39,235
[sighs] Did you find it?
But before you say anything…

406
00:29:39,694 --> 00:29:42,781
I want to thank you
for saving me from Raul.

407
00:29:43,406 --> 00:29:44,824
It's nothing, Governor. Just doing my job.

408
00:29:46,367 --> 00:29:48,912
Did you do what I asked you to do?

409
00:29:49,871 --> 00:29:53,583
There were no charred remains
in the building. Not one.

410
00:29:53,666 --> 00:29:56,002
That's impossible! Keep looking!

411
00:29:56,085 --> 00:29:59,297
Don't stop until you can
show me a dead body.

412
00:29:59,380 --> 00:30:00,298
Understand?

413
00:30:00,381 --> 00:30:02,717
I'm sorry, Governor.
I've checked everywhere.

414
00:30:02,801 --> 00:30:05,637
I couldn't find anything there.
You can go there yourself.

415
00:30:07,430 --> 00:30:09,015
Even if you kill me here now,

416
00:30:09,098 --> 00:30:10,975
I still won't be able
to show you anything.

417
00:30:11,267 --> 00:30:15,271
No, I'll find her. And I won't stop

418
00:30:15,355 --> 00:30:18,566
until I wipe my enemies
off the face of the earth.

419
00:30:19,943 --> 00:30:23,738
Papa said all I do is have people killed.

420
00:30:24,572 --> 00:30:25,573
But you know?

421
00:30:25,657 --> 00:30:29,369
The easiest way to get rid
of your enemies is to kill them.

422
00:30:30,912 --> 00:30:35,875
Because when you have,
that means you've won.

423
00:30:35,959 --> 00:30:39,128
[dramatic music playing]

424
00:30:45,343 --> 00:30:46,427
Ivy, wait. Ivy.

425
00:30:48,888 --> 00:30:49,889
Ivy…

426
00:30:50,807 --> 00:30:51,891
Don't touch me.

427
00:30:53,351 --> 00:30:55,144
Ivy, please talk to me.

428
00:30:57,897 --> 00:30:59,190
What's going on?

429
00:31:05,238 --> 00:31:07,782
Do you know why my mother
is like this now?

430
00:31:12,537 --> 00:31:15,039
She was raped, Diego.

431
00:31:16,624 --> 00:31:17,667
[gasps]

432
00:31:18,751 --> 00:31:23,256
She was shot and buried alive.

433
00:31:26,426 --> 00:31:30,930
So, every time I see her suffering…

434
00:31:31,598 --> 00:31:37,979
I remember the people who made her suffer.

435
00:31:41,482 --> 00:31:43,067
Who did this to her?

436
00:31:45,528 --> 00:31:48,072
Ivy, tell me. Who did this to your mother?

437
00:31:56,164 --> 00:31:58,416
You know what, Diego? You should leave.

438
00:31:59,584 --> 00:32:00,585
No.

439
00:32:01,920 --> 00:32:04,756
I won't leave
until you tell me everything.

440
00:32:06,591 --> 00:32:08,051
Why did you come back?

441
00:32:08,551 --> 00:32:11,512
Why did you lie to me?
Who did this to your mother?

442
00:32:12,472 --> 00:32:14,307
Diego, stop it. Please leave.

443
00:32:15,016 --> 00:32:20,897
Ivy, whatever your plans are,
I'm here for you. I'll help you.

444
00:32:23,650 --> 00:32:25,568
Because you're the only one
who believed in me.

445
00:32:26,861 --> 00:32:28,279
Because you're my friend.

446
00:32:32,450 --> 00:32:33,618
And because I love you.

447
00:32:33,701 --> 00:32:38,081
[soft instrumental playing]

448
00:32:47,131 --> 00:32:49,384
You don't know what you're saying, Diego.

449
00:32:51,094 --> 00:32:52,261
I <i>love</i> you.

450
00:32:52,345 --> 00:32:55,515
["Sa'Yo" by Silent Sanctuary playing]

451
00:32:55,598 --> 00:32:59,310
I love you as Lily. I love you as Ivy.

452
00:33:00,645 --> 00:33:03,481
So, please, give me a chance to show I do.

453
00:33:03,898 --> 00:33:08,277
["Sa'Yo" by Silent Sanctuary playing]

454
00:33:14,242 --> 00:33:15,952
You can't love me, Diego.

455
00:33:18,997 --> 00:33:22,625
-Never.
-Why not? Tell me.

456
00:33:24,419 --> 00:33:29,215
["Sa'Yo" by Silent Sanctuary playing]

457
00:33:52,405 --> 00:33:58,286
["Sa'Yo" by Silent Sanctuary playing]

458
00:34:10,006 --> 00:34:12,216
[song fades]

459
00:34:12,884 --> 00:34:13,801
[Arnaldo] Sure, Grandpa.

460
00:34:13,885 --> 00:34:16,012
I'll make Ivy's acquaintances talk,

461
00:34:16,095 --> 00:34:19,057
and I won't stop
until I get the answers I want.

462
00:34:19,515 --> 00:34:24,562
And then, bring that woman here
to get things done.

463
00:34:24,645 --> 00:34:27,148
Let's find out if she's still loyal to us.

464
00:34:28,524 --> 00:34:29,567
I will, Grandpa.

465
00:34:34,447 --> 00:34:36,949
Emilia, are you lost?

466
00:34:38,451 --> 00:34:40,787
This isn't your house anymore, remember?

467
00:34:44,415 --> 00:34:48,920
Papa. I know you barred me
from entering this house,

468
00:34:49,003 --> 00:34:51,047
but can I talk to you?

469
00:34:54,550 --> 00:34:55,551
Speak.

470
00:35:00,807 --> 00:35:03,601
First, I'd like to apologize, Papa,

471
00:35:03,684 --> 00:35:05,937
for all the mistakes I made.

472
00:35:06,854 --> 00:35:11,359
I know I've made decisions
without asking your permission.

473
00:35:13,569 --> 00:35:15,738
I did it all because…

474
00:35:17,949 --> 00:35:20,576
I just want you to be proud of me, Papa.

475
00:35:22,370 --> 00:35:29,127
And, if you'll just give me
this one last chance, Papa…

476
00:35:30,169 --> 00:35:32,797
I will correct my mistakes.

477
00:35:33,339 --> 00:35:37,051
I could be the best daughter
that you'll ever have, Papa.

478
00:35:39,095 --> 00:35:41,264
[crying] Just one last chance, Papa.

479
00:35:42,598 --> 00:35:44,183
Please forgive me!

480
00:35:44,767 --> 00:35:45,768
[Emilia sniffles]

481
00:35:49,438 --> 00:35:51,315
I'm begging you, Papa!

482
00:35:57,363 --> 00:35:59,866
[Ivy] Doctor. How's my mother?

483
00:35:59,949 --> 00:36:02,493
Let's wait for the test results
from the hospital.

484
00:36:03,244 --> 00:36:06,122
But I have good news.
Her pain is under control.

485
00:36:07,999 --> 00:36:12,962
Um, Miss Aguas, would you recall
when her condition started?

486
00:36:14,088 --> 00:36:16,299
We were separated for 13 years, Doc.

487
00:36:16,382 --> 00:36:20,344
She was kidnapped, and a lot
of things happened after that.

488
00:36:20,428 --> 00:36:23,681
She was raped… and locked up in a house.

489
00:36:23,764 --> 00:36:26,142
She might have been drugged as well.

490
00:36:26,225 --> 00:36:27,894
That's why she's like this now.

491
00:36:27,977 --> 00:36:30,855
Mm… I must be honest with you, Miss Aguas.

492
00:36:30,938 --> 00:36:33,024
Thirteen years is a very long time.

493
00:36:33,107 --> 00:36:36,861
Curing her condition won't be that easy.

494
00:36:36,944 --> 00:36:41,282
Are you saying my mom
won't be able to remember me?

495
00:36:41,365 --> 00:36:46,996
Your mom has what we call
catatonic depression.

496
00:36:47,079 --> 00:36:51,459
And the effect of this condition
is mild temporary memory loss.

497
00:36:51,542 --> 00:36:55,004
So, it means she can only remember events

498
00:36:55,087 --> 00:36:57,298
before the traumatic experience.

499
00:36:57,381 --> 00:36:58,716
So, that means she won't be

500
00:36:58,799 --> 00:37:02,261
able to adapt to new information, then?

501
00:37:02,345 --> 00:37:03,512
She will have a hard time

502
00:37:03,596 --> 00:37:07,600
accepting and processing
new information and memories.

503
00:37:07,683 --> 00:37:08,809
But I can talk to her.

504
00:37:08,893 --> 00:37:12,104
She can understand me.
She can even comprehend things.

505
00:37:12,188 --> 00:37:13,356
That's good.

506
00:37:13,439 --> 00:37:15,983
If she's getting encouragement
from her loved ones,

507
00:37:16,067 --> 00:37:18,861
she might be able to remember past events

508
00:37:18,945 --> 00:37:20,696
and maybe store new memories.

509
00:37:25,243 --> 00:37:26,786
[Emilia crying]

510
00:37:28,496 --> 00:37:29,497
Emilia…

511
00:37:32,083 --> 00:37:35,795
You're such a bad actress. Stop it.

512
00:37:36,212 --> 00:37:39,674
Do you think you can sway me by kneeling?

513
00:37:39,757 --> 00:37:41,884
Get up. Get up!

514
00:37:41,968 --> 00:37:44,929
It's shameful to see a woman
kneeling like that.

515
00:37:46,472 --> 00:37:50,643
And besides, whoever gave you the idea

516
00:37:51,560 --> 00:37:54,313
that I would let you rule
over my town again?

517
00:37:55,940 --> 00:37:58,025
You can't even manage your own family,

518
00:37:58,776 --> 00:38:00,069
much less a town.

519
00:38:00,778 --> 00:38:04,615
Stop your illusions. Fix your life.

520
00:38:05,449 --> 00:38:08,369
That's precisely what
I'm doing right now, Papa.

521
00:38:08,452 --> 00:38:10,579
[exhales sharply] I'm fixing my life.

522
00:38:10,663 --> 00:38:14,166
But how can I do that if you
lock me up in the guest house?

523
00:38:15,459 --> 00:38:18,087
You insult my intelligence
with your stupidity.

524
00:38:19,171 --> 00:38:23,009
Stop this, Emilia. I don't want
to see your face anymore. Guard!

525
00:38:23,092 --> 00:38:25,011
-[Emilia] Papa, please.
-Hold it.

526
00:38:25,094 --> 00:38:26,012
-Wait. Hold on.
-Grandpa.

527
00:38:26,095 --> 00:38:27,054
-Stop.
-Please. That's enough.

528
00:38:27,888 --> 00:38:29,682
Don't side with your mother

529
00:38:30,349 --> 00:38:33,019
if you don't want her failures
to rub off on you.

530
00:38:33,728 --> 00:38:36,772
With all due respect,
she's the victim here.

531
00:38:37,773 --> 00:38:39,984
I don't think she's the one
who should be punished.

532
00:38:43,654 --> 00:38:45,448
You really want to help your mother?

533
00:38:47,241 --> 00:38:48,993
Don't wipe her tears.

534
00:38:50,328 --> 00:38:51,412
Fix her problems.

535
00:38:51,996 --> 00:38:54,415
[tense music playing]

536
00:38:54,874 --> 00:38:56,042
Guards.

537
00:38:56,125 --> 00:38:58,252
[tense music playing]

538
00:39:00,671 --> 00:39:01,964
[Emilia weeping]

539
00:39:14,643 --> 00:39:17,063
[Camia groans]

540
00:39:21,233 --> 00:39:23,444
-Mom?
-[Camia gasps]

541
00:39:23,527 --> 00:39:25,946
Mom. Mom, don't be scared.

542
00:39:27,531 --> 00:39:29,658
It's me. It's… It's Ivy.

543
00:39:31,452 --> 00:39:32,495
Ivy?

544
00:39:35,122 --> 00:39:36,665
Yes, Mom. Ivy.

545
00:39:39,043 --> 00:39:40,336
Do you remember me?

546
00:39:42,421 --> 00:39:45,174
But Ivy isn't my real name.

547
00:39:45,716 --> 00:39:48,427
My name was changed to Ivy
when I got adopted.

548
00:39:48,511 --> 00:39:52,556
My real name is Lily.

549
00:39:54,308 --> 00:39:55,976
Mom, it's me. I'm Lily.

550
00:39:56,685 --> 00:40:00,523
Your daughter, Lily. Do you remember me?

551
00:40:01,524 --> 00:40:02,483
No.

552
00:40:04,318 --> 00:40:06,278
You're not my daughter Lily.

553
00:40:08,155 --> 00:40:09,156
But…

554
00:40:10,699 --> 00:40:11,700
But you…

555
00:40:14,453 --> 00:40:16,080
when the house was burning…

556
00:40:20,084 --> 00:40:21,127
you helped me.

557
00:40:25,381 --> 00:40:26,841
You saved my life.

558
00:40:28,676 --> 00:40:30,761
Thank you, Ivy.

559
00:40:36,100 --> 00:40:37,852
There was another man, right?

560
00:40:39,311 --> 00:40:40,729
He helped us too.

561
00:40:46,861 --> 00:40:47,862
It was Diego.

562
00:40:49,613 --> 00:40:50,448
Where is he?

563
00:40:51,866 --> 00:40:53,742
I want to thank him too.

564
00:40:59,999 --> 00:41:01,000
Diego.

565
00:41:02,168 --> 00:41:03,461
Don't leave yet.

566
00:41:05,838 --> 00:41:07,631
My mother wants to see you.

567
00:41:22,938 --> 00:41:24,857
[crying]

568
00:41:26,442 --> 00:41:30,905
Camia, I know… I know you're still alive.

569
00:41:31,322 --> 00:41:32,698
[Ivy] Careful, Mom.

570
00:41:36,076 --> 00:41:37,077
Mom…

571
00:41:38,412 --> 00:41:40,122
he's the man who helped us.

572
00:41:42,917 --> 00:41:44,710
[Raul] I know you're still alive.

573
00:41:45,169 --> 00:41:46,170
[sniffles]

574
00:41:46,962 --> 00:41:47,963
I…

575
00:41:48,631 --> 00:41:50,132
I love you so much.

576
00:41:53,677 --> 00:41:55,513
Thank you for helping us.

577
00:41:56,430 --> 00:41:57,973
That was very kind of you.

578
00:41:59,141 --> 00:42:00,893
You, Ivy, and you…

579
00:42:01,644 --> 00:42:02,645
Diego.

580
00:42:04,772 --> 00:42:08,192
I'll always be here for you and Ivy.

581
00:42:20,454 --> 00:42:21,580
[groans]

582
00:42:22,498 --> 00:42:23,791
-Mom?
-It hurts.

583
00:42:24,083 --> 00:42:27,002
-You're having a headache?
-Yes.

584
00:42:27,086 --> 00:42:29,797
[Ivy] Where does it hurt? Okay. Come here.

585
00:42:29,880 --> 00:42:31,423
-Mrs. Camia.
-[Ivy] Get some rest.

586
00:42:32,258 --> 00:42:33,801
Mrs. Camia, are you okay?

587
00:42:35,094 --> 00:42:36,095
Mrs. Camia?

588
00:42:36,262 --> 00:42:38,013
[breathes heavily]

589
00:42:38,097 --> 00:42:40,015
[tense music playing]

590
00:42:40,099 --> 00:42:41,100
Mrs. Camia?

591
00:42:46,021 --> 00:42:49,942
[tense music continues playing]

592
00:42:53,153 --> 00:42:54,572
<i>You're more beautiful up close.</i>

593
00:42:54,655 --> 00:42:55,864
<i>Sir, please take your hands off me.</i>

594
00:42:55,948 --> 00:42:57,032
<i>I'm just saying you're beautiful.</i>

595
00:42:57,116 --> 00:42:58,534
<i>I said take your hands off me!</i>

596
00:42:58,617 --> 00:43:01,036
<i>Don't touch me! Let me go! Let me go!</i>

597
00:43:01,370 --> 00:43:04,999
[tense music playing]

598
00:43:06,333 --> 00:43:07,960
-[Camia screams]
-Mom! Mom.

599
00:43:08,043 --> 00:43:10,921
-You bastard! Get away from me!
-Mrs. Camia!

600
00:43:11,005 --> 00:43:12,047
Mom, he helped us!

601
00:43:12,131 --> 00:43:13,299
-[Diego] Mrs. Camia.
-[screams] Raul, you bastard!

602
00:43:13,382 --> 00:43:15,884
If it weren't for you,
I wouldn't be like this!

603
00:43:15,968 --> 00:43:18,804
Get away from me! Leave! Leave!

604
00:43:18,887 --> 00:43:20,514
Doc! Mom! Mom! Mom!

605
00:43:20,598 --> 00:43:23,100
-[Dr. Faustino] Take her inside.
-[Camia] Let me go!

606
00:43:23,183 --> 00:43:26,395
-Careful!
-[Camia] Ouch! Ouch!

607
00:43:27,354 --> 00:43:28,355
[Ivy] Mom!

608
00:43:28,480 --> 00:43:31,692
[tense music playing]

609
00:43:32,318 --> 00:43:34,570
Let me go! [screams]

610
00:43:34,653 --> 00:43:36,071
-Be careful.
-Let me go!

611
00:43:36,155 --> 00:43:38,490
-[Ivy] Mom. Mom.
-[Camia screaming]

612
00:43:38,574 --> 00:43:39,908
-Put her down.
-[Camia screams]

613
00:43:39,992 --> 00:43:41,869
-Stop!
-Mom.

614
00:43:42,661 --> 00:43:44,705
[screaming]

615
00:43:47,666 --> 00:43:50,085
[Dr. Faustino] It's okay. Just relax.

616
00:43:50,336 --> 00:43:51,462
[Camia screams]

617
00:43:53,047 --> 00:43:55,716
Doc, what's happening?
What's happening to my mother?

618
00:43:55,799 --> 00:43:58,677
Seeing Diego might've triggered a memory.

619
00:43:59,011 --> 00:44:01,597
These memories are confusing for her,

620
00:44:01,680 --> 00:44:03,265
so the more she tries to understand them,

621
00:44:03,349 --> 00:44:06,393
the more her brain is in
overdrive and gets strained.

622
00:44:06,477 --> 00:44:07,686
That explains her behavior.

623
00:44:08,062 --> 00:44:09,271
So, what do you suggest?

624
00:44:09,355 --> 00:44:12,107
We can't tell her anything about the past?

625
00:44:12,441 --> 00:44:14,985
[Dr. Faustino] Not exactly.
But it shouldn't be abrupt.

626
00:44:15,069 --> 00:44:18,781
The unfolding of memories
should be gradual, or else,

627
00:44:18,864 --> 00:44:21,575
she'll get stressed.
Stress triggers anxiety.

628
00:44:21,659 --> 00:44:24,161
So, tell me. What should we do?

629
00:44:24,662 --> 00:44:28,791
Well, we can do therapy, gradual therapy,

630
00:44:28,874 --> 00:44:30,959
so she can regain her buried memories.

631
00:44:31,043 --> 00:44:33,712
Okay, Doc. We will do whatever it takes.

632
00:44:33,796 --> 00:44:36,674
We'll do everything for my mom to recover.

633
00:44:37,800 --> 00:44:39,093
Yes, we'll do that.

634
00:44:46,684 --> 00:44:48,185
[Raul crying]

635
00:44:55,484 --> 00:44:56,402
[sniffles]

636
00:45:01,907 --> 00:45:04,118
Is that because you feel guilty
for hurting Mom?

637
00:45:06,078 --> 00:45:08,080
Or sad that your mistress is dead?

638
00:45:09,206 --> 00:45:10,916
[tense music playing]

639
00:45:11,834 --> 00:45:13,252
In case you don't know…

640
00:45:15,254 --> 00:45:17,005
you're a good-for-nothing husband.

641
00:45:17,089 --> 00:45:19,174
[tense music playing]

642
00:45:19,258 --> 00:45:21,427
and in my opinion…

643
00:45:23,762 --> 00:45:25,180
you're a worthless father too.

644
00:45:26,849 --> 00:45:29,601
Do you understand? Don't ever forget that.

645
00:45:32,771 --> 00:45:36,316
Mom keeps killing people because of you.

646
00:45:36,900 --> 00:45:38,235
What do you do in return?

647
00:45:40,070 --> 00:45:43,031
You know, Arnaldo, I'm your father.

648
00:45:44,158 --> 00:45:46,702
You shouldn't talk to me that way.

649
00:45:47,369 --> 00:45:48,996
-You don't understand that--
-Really?

650
00:45:50,664 --> 00:45:51,832
Father?

651
00:45:55,544 --> 00:45:56,545
No.

652
00:45:58,464 --> 00:46:00,048
Just so we're clear…

653
00:46:01,550 --> 00:46:02,968
Just so we're clear,

654
00:46:04,553 --> 00:46:06,555
I gave up on you a long time ago.

655
00:46:06,638 --> 00:46:09,975
[tense music playing]

656
00:46:15,105 --> 00:46:16,231
[exhales]

657
00:46:21,111 --> 00:46:23,071
-Please take care of her.
-Okay.

658
00:46:28,160 --> 00:46:30,829
Ivy. Is it true, Ivy?

659
00:46:33,373 --> 00:46:38,545
Is it true my dad's the reason
your mother's this way now?

660
00:46:40,422 --> 00:46:41,632
Answer me, Ivy.

661
00:46:44,092 --> 00:46:45,344
Is it true?

662
00:46:46,261 --> 00:46:49,139
Lily, please answer my question.
Tell me the truth.

663
00:46:52,017 --> 00:46:53,977
Ivy. Please tell me.

664
00:46:54,061 --> 00:46:55,646
You want the truth?!

665
00:46:56,939 --> 00:46:58,732
You want answers?!

666
00:46:59,233 --> 00:47:00,567
Didn't you hear her?

667
00:47:01,860 --> 00:47:05,697
Yes! My mother is like that
because of Raul!

668
00:47:06,281 --> 00:47:08,492
Because of your good-for-nothing father!

669
00:47:08,575 --> 00:47:12,371
[dramatic music playing]

670
00:47:15,165 --> 00:47:16,708
[Emilia] <i>I need to find out who</i>

671
00:47:16,792 --> 00:47:18,001
<i>filed the police report against Raul.</i>

672
00:47:18,085 --> 00:47:20,379
<i>Do you know what Jasmin's full name is?</i>

673
00:47:20,462 --> 00:47:23,215
<i>Camia Cruz, a woman</i>
<i>Mom killed a long time ago.</i>

674
00:47:23,298 --> 00:47:24,174
<i>She's still alive.</i>

675
00:47:24,258 --> 00:47:26,552
[Emilia] <i>Because I'm the one</i>
<i>who had her killed,</i>

676
00:47:26,635 --> 00:47:29,638
<i>I need to bury her back</i>
<i>in the grave she crawled out of!</i>

677
00:47:29,721 --> 00:47:31,515
[Diego] <i>If it weren't for your womanizing,</i>

678
00:47:31,598 --> 00:47:34,643
<i>none of this would've happened</i>
<i>to Lily or our family!</i>

679
00:47:34,726 --> 00:47:35,686
[Raul] <i>Wait, what family?</i>

680
00:47:35,769 --> 00:47:37,604
<i>You aren't related to the Ardientes.</i>

681
00:47:38,188 --> 00:47:39,898
[Jepoy] <i>We need to keep a</i>
<i>closer eye on your mom.</i>

682
00:47:39,982 --> 00:47:42,526
<i>Emilia knows she was</i>
<i>in that burning house.</i>

683
00:47:42,609 --> 00:47:44,069
<i>-And she suspects that she's still alive.</i>
<i>-Does she?</i>

684
00:47:44,152 --> 00:47:47,948
<i>Then I need to be ready in case</i>
<i>Emilia figures us out.</i>

685
00:47:48,031 --> 00:47:51,285
[theme music playing]
